log / exp of ARM Optimized Routines as built into glibc 2.39 (patches/0450)
  patches/0450-glm-gpu-round.patch (glm5_next/cuda/gpusample.py) re-implements, for the GPU, the float64 log and
  exp that numpy calls on aarch64: glibc 2.39's __log / __exp (sysdeps/ieee754/dbl-64/e_log.c, e_exp.c), which come
  from ARM's Optimized Routines (https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines, math/log.c, math/exp.c;
  Copyright (c) Arm Limited; MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception). The algorithm and its coefficient / lookup
  tables (e_log_data.c / e_exp_data.c, read from Ubuntu's libm.so.6 2.39-0ubuntu8.9 binary and equal to those
  sources) are reproduced so that the GPU sampler's bits equal the host's; the instruction order follows the
  binary. tests/libm_a64.py compares against that binary, which each user downloads.

Public text behind the shipped draft vocabulary ranking (patches/0420)
  The token ranking draft_vocab.txt in patches/0420-glm-draft-vocab.patch holds token ids ordered by frequency,
  counted by bench/draftvocab_public.py in: OpenAssistant/oasst1 (Apache-2.0), SWE-Gym/OpenHands-SFT-Trajectories
  (MIT), CPython 3.14.7 Lib/ and Doc/ (PSF License 2.0), denoland/std (MIT) and BurntSushi/ripgrep 14.1.1 (MIT OR
  Unlicense), at the revisions pinned in that script. No text of these sources is included, only token counts'
  order.

